OL,3,GNEWSAMan with scalded foot rescued from
OL,4,APeak District
OL,5,
OL,6,FA hiker was rescued from one of the
OL,7,FPeak District's most popular spots
OL,8,Fafter scalding himself with hot water.
OL,10,FKinder Mountain Rescue Team said the
OL,11,Fwalker was part of a group on Kinder
OL,12,FScout that had stopped for some food at
OL,13,Fabout 14:40 BST on Saturday, when "he
OL,14,Fmanaged to [accidentally] spill hot
OL,15,Fwater which went inside his boot and
OL,16,Fscalded his foot".
OL,23,APub: 23-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (E) NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,363,360,200,160,0,100
